 "text": "Hello, how are you holding up? Pick them up one at a time, keeping them relatively light. Most people grocery shop this way, using the front basket for bread and the bag for fruit. If you need carry several items, a basket can be very helpful. Full it up then and you won't overwork your arms. Then aim to split it up whenever you shop, so each trip is shorter and easier. A backpack weighs a bit, and it' easy to fall off a bike. Stick to simple shop shop trips and use a basket.",
